<caml:Content xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#"><p>Each agency shall maintain all records, to the maximum extent possible, with accuracy, relevance, timeliness, and completeness.</p><p>Such standard need not be met except when such records are used to make any determination about the individual. When an agency transfers a record outside of state government, it shall correct, update, withhold, or delete any portion of the record that it knows or has reason to believe is inaccurate or untimely.</p></caml:Content>